 "definition": "Retrospective, post hoc: rung 2's r_decay (code/e6_r2.py) on the 108 runs of the delivered E2 MLP arm (code/e2.py,\nexp = mlp: f(x) = W2 tanh(W1 x), H = 128, n = d = 64, minibatch SGD B = 64 on sampled fields and masks, P0 = p0 I,\ndecay lam on W1, W2 and P). Inputs only: no training is re-run. The truths (rank_meas, #sv(W2) > 0.05 at t_end) were\nknown, and r_decay was developed after E2's result on the rung-2 development grids.\n\nPer run, from its own seed (code/e2.py mlp_init: W1(0), W2(0), P0) and the delivered Monte Carlo sample of the hidden\nstatistics (feature_stats: rng 10^6 + seed, 2e5 draws in chunks of 1e4, same draw order):\n  r_init_check  linjepa.n1_general on the statistics at initialisation = the delivered rank_pred; recomputed here as a\n                reproduction check of the inputs (must equal the delivered value on every run)\n  r_decay       e6_r2.n1g_tv with the statistics of W1(t) = (1 - eta lam)^step W1(0), recomputed every STAT_EVERY = 50\n                steps (as rung 2), same integrator, check spacing (10) and count (maximum over checks) as N1-general.\n                The statistics depend on W1 only through the scalar a = (1 - eta lam)^step, so S(a) is computed on the\n                fixed Monte Carlo sample at a grid of log a (step DLOG = 0.1, from 0 to log A_LIN) and S(a)/a^2 is\n                interpolated linearly in log a; below A_LIN, S(a) = a^2 S(A_LIN) / A_LIN^2 (tanh linear there;\n                pre-activation sd times A_LIN is recorded per run).\nNot in r_decay: the SGD noise in W1's drift (W1 moves by gradient noise of order |W2| and by minibatch sampling), the\nmasks' sampling noise in W2's own dynamics, and any W1 learning once W2 has grown.\nCompared on the same 108 runs with the delivered r_init (2.69) and the mu variants of results/baselines/dvd_e2_runs.csv\n(dvd_signed 1.90, dvd_exact 1.91, dvd_pq 9.44): MAE, within-1, bias, exceed (share of runs with truth > count), pooled\nand per mask family; 